And here is why...

This is a story of a young knight named KingThomas, who once dreamed
of getting the high score on my school's nethakc server.  I have never
ascended before, and this was my most promising character yet.  I had
found the vibrating square, had ascension kit complete except for ring
of conflict, but I did have a +6 grayswandir, and -34 ac, and magic
missile was averaging over 100 damage, which allowed me to one or two
shot many deadly monsters with it.  Yeah, liches?  I could two shot
them, given a wall.  I even let some summon a bunch of creatures when
I was fighting one of the deamon princes, just so I could see if I
would need one of my 8 blessed potions of full healing that I had.
Many D and h corpses later, I had not been below half health.  I
thought I was unkillable...  Until I decided to try to start the game
in wizard mode.

$nethack -D -u wizard
shall I pick your race and class for you? (y/n) n
etc.
got into the game, where it said it could not enter wizard mode
because I had to be named "wizard" instead of Wizard.

SO, I decided to just name myself that at the prompt.
$nethack -D
restoring saved file...

of course, in my rcfile, I had specified -u KingThomas, because that
was the only character I was playing.  I had just opened the game in
debug mode.  Panicking, I exit the terminal.  To no avail.  I believe
the game is lost for good.  This is why you should keep a save file.
Or just not be a complete idiot.


